All 4 test cases pass, matching the expected values from the Zephyr unit test suite. The implementation is complete.

**Summary:** Implemented `crc4()` in `subsys/crc/crc4_sw.c`. The function computes a 4-bit CRC by processing each byte as two nibbles (MSB first), then performing 4 bit-shift steps per nibble. When `reversed` is true, it processes LSB-first (checking bit 0, shifting right); otherwise MSB-first (checking bit 3, shifting left). The result is masked to 4 bits (`& 0xF`).


